    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d116">

                <pb facs="0206" n="120" sameAs="frus:frus1927v01/pg120"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15 a 1/457: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chairman of the American
                        Delegation</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-07-20T15:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20, 1927—3
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>57. Your No. 110, July 19, midnight. After my telegram to Houghton last
                        week,<anchor n="73" xml:id="d116-f1"/> it is somewhat embarrassing to take
                    matter up <pb facs="0207" n="121" xml:id="pg121"/> again with British
                    Government. I am willing, however, to do anything that will be of assistance in
                    bringing about an agreement.</p>
                <p>In regard to your suggestions, the first seems to be taken care of by my telegram
                    to Houghton; do not fully understand the second.</p>
                <p>If I go no further than to say to the British that we cannot accept limitation of
                    unit displacement of cruisers which would preclude armament of efficient battery
                    of 8-inch guns, would not British assume that we are willing to make agreement
                    to build cruisers below 10,000 tons with 8-inch guns?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d116-f1" n="73" xml:id="d116-f1-content">
                <p>Quoted in telegram No. 50, July 16, 1 p.m., to the chairman of the American
                    delegation, <ref target="#pg108">p. 108</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
